{
  "toolkit": "Modernizer Widgets",
  "about": "One entry per widget. view: name in the Coach Designer palette; binding: the bound System Data type, or null; label: the view has a Label property; options: configuration options (type: a System Data type or NameValuePair; list: a list of them; group: the Configuration section Coach Designer shows it in, as the UI Toolkit's Behavior, Items and Appearance; an option the UI Toolkit also has takes its UI Toolkit name, so the modernizer can carry its value over); events: the view's events, listed in Coach Designer's Events tab, each with the names of the arguments its handler gets, as the UI Toolkit names them (labels: the top-level events); accessor: the UI Toolkit's names of the getter and setter a handler calls on me for the widget's value (its label when it has no binding), as isChecked and setChecked on a Checkbox; boundary: fires the view's boundary event; preview: the value a Coach Designer preview shows; uiToolkit: the UI Toolkit control the widget stands for, whose settings and events it has (ui-toolkit-reference.json); leftOut: the counterpart's settings and events it does not have, each with the reason; tags: palette categories (Coach Designer lists Input, Informational, Layout, Operational and Chart; the toolkit's name is added so a palette search for it lists every widget). A new widget needs only its component (coach-ui/src/widgets/<kind>.jsx), its entry here and its icon (icons/<kind>.svg), plus coach-ui/src/widgets/<kind>.scss when it uses a Carbon component the stock widgets do not: the build, the harness, the inspector and the modernizer read this file and that folder.",
